<title>USA: Georgia hires firms to pursue overdue taxes.</title>
<headline>Georgia hires firms to pursue overdue taxes.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Department of Revenue said Tuesday it has hired three private firms to pursue $250 million of delinquent tax collections.</p>
<p>The agency has signed contracts with Equifax Risk Management Services, a unit of Equifax Inc, Nationwide Recovery Service and Payco-General American Credits, a unit of Payco American Corp.</p>
<p>Revenue Commissioner Jerry Jackson said the state would turn over to the agencies 50,000 delinquent accounts worth $250 million next month.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
